<title>SWEDEN: Electrolux 9-mo profit falls 13 pct.</title>
<headline>Electrolux 9-mo profit falls 13 pct.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1996-10-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish appliance maker Electrolux posts results for the nine months ending September 30, 1996.</p>
<p>					(million crowns unless stated)</p>
<p> Profit after fin items		 2,418  vs  2,783</p>
<p> Sales				     82,923  vs 88,822</p>
<p> Earnings per share (SKR)	     18.30  vs  23.10</p>
<p> Operating costs			 76,296  vs 81,573</p>
<p> Operating income before deprec     6,627  vs  7,249</p>
<p> Depreciation			     3,312  vs  3,364</p>
<p> Operating profit after deprec	3,315  vs  3,885</p>
<p> Net financial items	  CHARGE    897  vs  1,102  CHARGE</p>
<p> Minorities				   230  vs     51</p>
<p> Pre-tax profit			   2,188  vs  2,732</p>
<p> Tax					    846  vs  1,041</p>
<p> Net profit				 1,342  vs  1,691</p>
<p>NOTE -- A Reuter poll of 10 analysts found Electrolux was expected to post a profit after financial items of 2.46 billion crowns for the first nine months of 1996.</p>
<p>-- Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700 1017</p>
</text>
